steps.bodyMd:
A person's effective permissions are the **union** of four sources:

1. their own organisation role;
2. permissions set directly on any group they belong to;
3. roles attached to those groups;
4. a group's own **Group Role**, which fans a role out to every member.

Grants only add. Nothing in this stack subtracts, so an over-broad role cannot be repaired by moving someone into a narrower group — you change the role, or nothing changes. Underneath it all, every signed-in account keeps chat access.

One setting runs the other way: a group's **Allowed tiers** limits which model tiers — which classes of AI model — its members may pick. That limit lives in the group, so membership of a second, unrestricted group widens it again.
